# The spill tier's bookkeeping off the engine loop. A kept state made its own room on the engine's loop as it was kept
# (patch 0110's persist): its conversation's quota (its own old turns and forks past its share of the cap, _trim_own) and
# the cap's or the free-disk floor's shortfall (_make_room), each walking every stored state, and the quota every block
# name of every stored point, while every stream waited. Room grows with the store: at 768 GiB a Spark it holds about
# twelve times the states of the 64 GiB the tier was measured at. Now the keep only checks counters (a state the disk
# cannot hold whatever goes is still refused there, at once); when room or a quota is wanted, the writer makes it before
# the state's first byte is written, in the same eviction order (a job queued ahead of the state's rows: the writer
# takes its jobs in order). Still short then, the state is not written: counted as no_space, its blocks never staged.
# A conversation's bytes for its quota are counted from its own points against the blocks' reference counts, which
# count every stored point and waiting state naming a block: exactly what walking every block name gave, for the
# points' own blocks only. /health's room_s: the writer's time making room. mgllm, 2026-10-13.
# Tests: tests/test_9023_spill_bookkeeping.py (CPU), and the recipe's tools/spill_blocks_check.py (73 checks, all pass).

